Each path is an isometry on the incoming field space. For a fixed marked edge and sign, different c have different occupied-B words, so their output ranges are orthogonal. The two signs have different A charges and are also orthogonal for every diagonal charge function. Thus all initial tested jump kernels are scalar multiples of P0, independent of the field density. No interference between separately recorded edges is introduced. In particular the total initial loss is

\[
