\lambda_0=2\kappa\sum_a d_a(d_a-1).                        \tag{11}
\]

Summing (10) over sigma gives 2(f_c-f_a); summing the ordered b!=c choices gives (1). For u_b=f_b-f_a and v_b=g_b-g_a,

\[
\sum_{\sigma=\pm1}\overline{(u_c-\sigma u_b)}(v_c-\sigma v_b)
=2(\bar u_c v_c+\bar u_b v_b).
