Each neighbor occurs d_a-1 times in each position. Therefore the derivative of the raw second moment is (2). Since both means vanish at time zero, the derivative of their product vanishes; the connected covariance has the same derivative. In particular the variance is not being conflated with a Fisher information or a finite-frequency spectrum.

